@Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5047
@ClientToken = paste-client-jwt-here
@AdminToken = paste-admin-jwt-here
@TicketId = paste-ticket-id-here

### Swagger UI check
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/swagger/index.html

### Register client
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Client",
  "companyName": "Test Company",
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "Password12345",
  "confirmPassword": "Password12345"
}

### Login client
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "Password12345"
}

### Login admin
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@forcebit.be",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### Client creates ticket
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{ClientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer does not work",
  "category": "Question",
  "subject": "Software",
  "initialMessage": "The printer software opens, but printing never starts."
}

### Client lists own tickets
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{ClientToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Admin lists all tickets
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/admin/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{AdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Get ticket detail
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/{{TicketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{AdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Admin replies to ticket
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/{{TicketId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{AdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Thanks for reporting this. We are checking the printer software settings."
}

### Reply with attachments
# Replace the file path with a real local png, jpg, pdf, or zip file.
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/{{TicketId}}/messages/with-attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{AdminToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=replyBoundary

--replyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="message"

Here is a reply with an attachment.
--replyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="example.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./example.pdf
--replyBoundary--

### Admin sets status to In Progress
PATCH {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/{{TicketId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{AdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "InProgress"
}

### Admin closes ticket
PATCH {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/{{TicketId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{AdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Closed"
}

### Client reopens ticket
PATCH {{Api_HostAddress}}/api/tickets/{{TicketId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{ClientToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Open"
}
